-- SHADOW-SEMANTICS cell I13 (S1 scope, ruling #1375): the i12 shape with a LIVE
-- IMPL at the receiver's head tycon, which is the direction that shows the clause
-- changing what a WRITABLE name denotes.
--
-- `size` here is the `Int -> Int` standalone this module explicitly imported from
-- `prov`, and `Box` comes from `boxmod`; `Sizeable` and `impl Sizeable Box` live
-- in `ifcmod`, which reaches the graph only through `bridge`'s plain import and
-- is therefore NOT nameable here.  So `size` is not a shadow in this module, the
-- occurrence is the imported `Int -> Int` standalone, and applying it to a `Box`
-- is a located REJECT (`Type mismatch: Int vs Box`) on all three verbs.
--
-- Under the graph-global reading the same source is ACCEPTED at exit 0 and prints
-- `300` -- an impl body from a module with no import path to here, selected for a
-- receiver the name the author actually wrote cannot even accept.  Unlike i12 the
-- wrong answer is not merely a different number: it is only reachable through a
-- denotation this module cannot write down.
import boxmod.{Box(..)}
import prov.{size}
import bridge.{bf}

main = println (size (Box 3) + bf 0)
